{"adr":"Minimal APIs mapped at contract paths with UsePathBase(\"/api\"), EF Core SQLite entities (EnsureCreated, no migrations), DTO records named after the contract schemas, and OpenAPI transformers to reach exact conformance (servers /api, inline enums, nullable allOf, required lists).\nStored session counts are totals that include the demo member. Rule failures throw ApiException, and one handler maps it, BadHttpRequest and any other exception to the contract Error (500 = storage_failure). Empty 404/405 responses go through status-code pages.\nOpen spec points are resolved like this. joinWaitlist order follows the assumptions (already_booked after outside_booking_window). Studio-cancelled Booked records go to Past and don't count toward the limit of 10 or stats.upcoming. Simulate never lowers a count below zero (bookedCount not below the demo member's own Booked row). Undo is refused for promoted records.\nStartup: TimeProvider is registered with TryAdd. Schema creation and seeding are skipped under GetDocument.Insider, and when they fail the error is caught and logged so requests return 500 storage_failure. Seeding runs only when the Sessions table is empty, with 4–12 sessions placed relative to the London day.\nNo new packages and no changes to the csproj, contract or CI.","chosen":"OPT-A","complexity":"L","header":{"createdAt":"2026-10-07T00:01:06.553Z","inputsHash":"","kind":"plan","producedBy":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","stage":"plan"},"runId":"20261006-boutique-fitness-studio-class-31fe","schemaVersion":1},"newDependencies":[],"options":[{"id":"OPT-A","simplest":false,"summary":"Layered minimal API. EF Core entities in App.Api/Data. Contract DTO records named exactly like the contract schemas. Scoped services: a projection (labels/actionState), queries and booking commands. Endpoints declare the contract's statuses with Produces. A small set of OpenAPI transformers aligns the generated document with contracts/openapi.yaml. One exception handler maps errors to the contract Error.","tradeoffs":"More files, but the rules can be read and reviewed in one place (BookingCommands), the projection is shared by every operation that returns a Session, and Program.cs stays thin. The OpenAPI transformers are the main risk and get their own task."},{"id":"OPT-B","simplest":true,"summary":"Everything inline: the 13 endpoint lambdas in Program.cs query AppDb directly and build anonymous/DTO objects in place, with no service layer.","tradeoffs":"Fewest files. But the actionState, label and late-flag logic would be copied across about 8 operations. Program.cs would grow to 800+ lines, and the work can't be split into tasks whose file scopes don't overlap."},{"id":"OPT-C","simplest":false,"summary":"Like OPT-A, but a document transformer loads contracts/openapi.yaml and returns it as the generated document.","tradeoffs":"The conformance check passes trivially, but it no longer catches drift between the code and the contract, so it defeats NFR-6. Rejected."}],"protectedPathsDeclared":[],"stubs":[{"content":"using System.Text.Json.Serialization;\n\nnamespace App.Api;\n\n[JsonConverter(typeof(JsonStringEnumConverter<ClassType>))]\npublic enum ClassType { Yoga, Pilates, HIIT, Spin, Boxing }\n\n[JsonConverter(typeof(JsonStringEnumConverter<Intensity>))]\npublic enum Intensity { Low, Medium, High }\n\n[JsonConverter(typeof(JsonStringEnumConverter<Room>))]\npublic enum Room\n{\n    [JsonStringEnumMemberName(\"Studio A\")] StudioA,\n    [JsonStringEnumMemberName(\"Studio B\")] StudioB,\n    [JsonStringEnumMemberName(\"Spin Room\")] SpinRoom\n}\n\n[JsonConverter(typeof(JsonStringEnumConverter<TimeOfDay>))]\npublic enum TimeOfDay { Morning, Afternoon, Evening }\n\n[JsonConverter(typeof(JsonStringEnumConverter<SessionStatus>))]\npublic enum SessionStatus\n{\n    Scheduled,\n    [JsonStringEnumMemberName(\"Cancelled by studio\")] CancelledByStudio\n}\n\n[JsonConverter(typeof(JsonStringEnumConverter<BookingStatus>))]\npublic enum BookingStatus\n{\n    Booked,\n    Waitlisted,\n    Cancelled,\n    Attended,\n    [JsonStringEnumMemberName(\"Cancelled by studio\")] CancelledByStudio\n}\n","path":"App.Api/Data/Enums.cs","reason":"New enums used by entities, DTOs and by tests that insert session/booking rows directly."},{"content":"namespace App.Api.Data;\n\npublic class InstructorEntity\n{\n    public int Id { get; set; }\n    public string Name { get; set; } = \"\";\n    public string Bio { get; set; } = \"\";\n    public string AvatarUrl { get; set; } = \"\";\n}\n\npublic class WhatToBringEntry\n{\n    public string Title { get; set; } = \"\";\n    public string Note { get; set; } = \"\";\n}\n\npublic class SessionEntity\n{\n    public int Id { get; set; }\n    public string Name { get; set; } = \"\";\n    public ClassType Type { get; set; }\n    public Intensity Intensity { get; set; }\n    public int InstructorId { get; set; }\n    public InstructorEntity? Instructor { get; set; }\n    public Room Room { get; set; }\n    /// <summary>UTC.</summary>\n    public DateTime StartsAt { get; set; }\n    /// <summary>UTC.</summary>\n    public DateTime EndsAt { get; set; }\n    public int Capacity { get; set; }\n    /// <summary>Total booked, including the demo member.</summary>\n    public int BookedCount { get; set; }\n    /// <summary>Total waiting, including the demo member.</summary>\n    public int WaitlistCount { get; set; }\n    public string Description { get; set; } = \"\";\n    public List<WhatToBringEntry> WhatToBring { get; set; } = new();\n    public SessionStatus Status { get; set; } = SessionStatus.Scheduled;\n}\n\npublic class BookingEntity\n{\n    public int Id { get; set; }\n    public int SessionId { get; set; }\n    public SessionEntity? Session { get; set; }\n    /// <summary>Stored values: Booked, Waitlisted or Cancelled.</summary>\n    public BookingStatus Status { get; set; }\n    public bool LateCancel { get; set; }\n    public int? WaitlistPosition { get; set; }\n    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }\n    public DateTime? CancelledAt { get; set; }\n    public DateTime? PromotedAt { get; set; }\n    public DateTime? NoticeAcknowledgedAt { get; set; }\n}\n","path":"App.Api/Data/Entities.cs","reason":"New entity types that rule tests use to insert sessions and bookings and to read rows (promoted-at, notice-acknowledged, status)."},{"content":"using App.Api.Data;\nusing Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;\n\nnamespace App.Api;\n\npublic class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\n{\n    public DbSet<InstructorEntity> Instructors => Set<InstructorEntity>();\n    public DbSet<SessionEntity> Sessions => Set<SessionEntity>();\n    public DbSet<BookingEntity> Bookings => Set<BookingEntity>();\n\n    protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder modelBuilder)\n    {\n        modelBuilder.Entity<SessionEntity>().OwnsMany(s => s.WhatToBring, b => b.ToJson());\n    }\n}\n","path":"App.Api/AppDb.cs","reason":"Adds the DbSets that tests use to seed state and inspect rows; model configuration is completed in TASK-1."},{"content":"using System.Text.Json.Serialization;\n\nnamespace App.Api.Contracts;\n\npublic sealed record Member(int Id, string Name, string Initials, string Membership);\n\npublic sealed record Instructor(int Id, string Name, string Bio, string AvatarUrl);\n\npublic sealed record WhatToBringItem(string Title, string Note);\n\npublic sealed record SkipReason(string Code, string Message);\n\npublic sealed record ActionState(\n    string Kind,\n    bool CanChange,\n    int? SpotsLeft,\n    int? Position,\n    int? BookingId,\n    string? Reason,\n    SkipReason? SkipReason,\n    bool? LateCancellation);\n\npublic sealed record Session(\n    int Id,\n    string Name,\n    ClassType Type,\n    Intensity Intensity,\n    Instructor Instructor,\n    Room Room,\n    DateTime StartsAt,\n    DateTime EndsAt,\n    int DurationMin,\n    int Capacity,\n    int BookedCount,\n    int WaitlistCount,\n    string Description,\n    IReadOnlyList<WhatToBringItem> WhatToBring,\n    SessionStatus Status,\n    string AvailabilityLabel,\n    string CapacityLabel,\n    ActionState ActionState,\n    int? MyBookingId);\n\npublic sealed record DaySummary(DateOnly Date, string Label, bool IsToday, bool HasSessions);\n\npublic sealed record Schedule(\n    DateOnly Today,\n    DateOnly Date,\n    DateOnly WeekStart,\n    bool CanGoPreviousWeek,\n    bool CanGoNextWeek,\n    IReadOnlyList<DaySummary> Days,\n    IReadOnlyList<Session> Sessions);\n\npublic sealed record SessionRequest\n{\n    [JsonRequired]\n    public int SessionId { get; init; }\n}\n\npublic sealed record Booking(\n    int Id,\n    int SessionId,\n    BookingStatus Status,\n    bool LateCancel,\n    int? WaitlistPosition,\n    SkipReason? SkipReason,\n    DateTime CreatedAt,\n    DateTime? CancelledAt);\n\npublic sealed record BookingChange(Booking Booking, Session Session, string Message);\n\npublic sealed record UndoResult(Session Session, string Message);\n\npublic sealed record SessionSummary(\n    int Id,\n    string Name,\n    ClassType Type,\n    string InstructorName,\n    Room Room,\n    DateTime StartsAt,\n    DateTime EndsAt,\n    int DurationMin);\n\npublic sealed record BookingRow(\n    int Id,\n    int SessionId,\n    BookingStatus Status,\n    bool LateCancel,\n    int? WaitlistPosition,\n    SkipReason? SkipReason,\n    string Badge,\n    bool CanChange,\n    bool IsLateIfCancelledNow,\n    SessionSummary Session);\n\npublic sealed record UpcomingGroup(string Label, DateOnly Date, IReadOnlyList<BookingRow> Rows);\n\npublic sealed record MyBookings(IReadOnlyList<UpcomingGroup> Upcoming, IReadOnlyList<BookingRow> Past);\n\npublic sealed record Stats(int Upcoming, int ClassesThisMonth, int CurrentStreakWeeks);\n\npublic sealed record PromotionNotice(int BookingId, int SessionId, string SessionName, DateTime StartsAt, string Message);\n\npublic sealed record PromotionNotices(IReadOnlyList<PromotionNotice> Notices);\n\npublic sealed record SimulationResult(Session Session, Booking? Booking);\n\npublic sealed record Error(string Code, string Message, Session? Session);\n","path":"App.Api/Contracts/Dtos.cs","reason":"New contract DTO records that tests may deserialize responses into; names match the contract schemas."}],"tasks":[{"approach":"Start from the stubs. Enums go in namespace App.Api: ClassType, Intensity, Room (Studio A / Studio B / Spin Room), TimeOfDay, SessionStatus (Scheduled / Cancelled by studio) and BookingStatus (Booked, Waitlisted, Cancelled, Attended, Cancelled by studio; only the first 3 are ever stored). Entities go in App.Api.Data: InstructorEntity, SessionEntity (StartsAt/EndsAt are UTC DateTime; Capacity, BookedCount and WaitlistCount are TOTALS that include the demo member; WhatToBring is a list of owned WhatToBringEntry stored as JSON via OwnsMany(...).ToJson(); Status) and BookingEntity (SessionId, Status, LateCancel, WaitlistPosition, CreatedAt, CancelledAt, PromotedAt, NoticeAcknowledgedAt). In AppDb add DbSets Instructors/Sessions/Bookings. In ConfigureConventions add a DateTime and DateTime? converter that writes UTC and reads with DateTimeKind.Utc. Store enums as strings (HaveConversion<string>()). No unique index (ASM-8).","conventions":["file-scoped namespaces","primary-constructor DbContext like the existing AppDb","enums carry JsonStringEnumConverter<T> plus JsonStringEnumMemberName for names with spaces"],"dependsOn":[],"exemplars":["App.Api/AppDb.cs","App.Api/Program.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/AppDb.cs","App.Api/Data/Entities.cs","App.Api/Data/Enums.cs"],"id":"TASK-1","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":120,"reqs":["REQ-38","REQ-7"],"title":"Data model: enums, entities, AppDb"},{"approach":"Keep the record shapes from the stub (namespace App.Api.Contracts). DateOnly is used for date fields and UTC DateTime for date-time fields. SessionRequest.SessionId is [JsonRequired], so a body of {} fails binding. Add ApiException(int status, string code, string message, Session? session = null) : Exception. Add static helpers for the codes used: NotFound(\"We couldn't find that class.\") / 404, Conflict(code, message, session?) / 409, Invalid() / 400 with the contract's plain messages. ActionState.Kind, SkipReason.Code and Error.Code stay strings; the OpenAPI task adds their inline enums.","conventions":["record type names equal the contract component schema names exactly (Member, Instructor, Session, Booking, Error, ...)","properties PascalCase, serialised camelCase by the default web JSON options","nullable fields are C# nullable so null is written, never omitted"],"dependsOn":["TASK-1"],"exemplars":["App.Api/AppDb.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Contracts/Dtos.cs","App.Api/Contracts/ApiException.cs"],"id":"TASK-2","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":140,"reqs":["REQ-1","NFR-1"],"title":"Contract DTOs and ApiException"},{"approach":"LondonTime is a static class over TimeZoneInfo.FindSystemTimeZoneById(\"Europe/London\"). It provides: ToLondon(utc), LondonDate(utc), WeekStart(DateOnly) for the Monday, StartOfLondonDayUtc(DateOnly), TimeOfDay(utc) (Morning < 12:00, Afternoon 12:00–16:59, Evening ≥ 17:00) and formatters DayTime \"ddd HH:mm\", Hm \"HH:mm\", DayLabel \"ddd d\" and GroupLabel \"ddd d MMM\". SessionProjection is a scoped class taking TimeProvider. ToSession(SessionEntity with Instructor, BookingEntity? demoActive) builds the contract Session: durationMin = minutes(EndsAt−StartsAt); spotsLeft = max(0, capacity−booked); capacityLabel \"{spots} of {cap} spots left\"; availabilityLabel is Cancelled for studio-cancelled, else \"Full · {waitlist} on waitlist\" when spots = 0 (including 0 waiting), else 1 → \"1 spot left\", 2–3 → \"Only N left\", ≥4 → \"N spots left\". actionState follows this order: (1) studio-cancelled → disabled, canChange false, reason \"Cancelled by studio\". (2) demo Booked → booked, bookingId, canChange = now < start, lateCancellation = start − now < 2h (false once started). (3) demo Waitlisted → waitlisted with position, canChange = now < start; if the class has ended, use disabled \"Class has started\" instead. (4) now ≥ start → disabled \"Class has started\". (5) start − now > 7d → disabled \"Booking opens 7 days before class\". (6) start − now < 15min → disabled \"Booking closes 15 minutes before class\". (7) full → join_waitlist with position waitlist + 1. (8) book with spotsLeft. Unused nullable fields are null; myBookingId = the held record's id. Also add ToBooking(BookingEntity) (skipReason always null) and ToRow(BookingEntity) for My Bookings. Display status: studio-cancelled session with Booked/Waitlisted → 'Cancelled by studio'; Booked and ended → Attended (the stored row is not changed). Badge is Booked | Waitlisted #N | Attended | Cancelled | Late cancel (Cancelled + LateCancel) | Cancelled by studio. canChange = (Booked or Waitlisted) and not started and session not studio-cancelled. isLateIfCancelledNow = Booked and not started and start − now < 2h.","conventions":["all 'now' comes from an injected TimeProvider (GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime); never DateTime.Now/UtcNow","rule numbers are const fields: BookingOpensDays=7, BookingClosesMinutes=15, LateCancelHours=2, UndoSeconds=5, UpcomingLimit=10","format with CultureInfo.InvariantCulture"],"dependsOn":["TASK-2"],"exemplars":["App.Api/AppDb.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Services/LondonTime.cs","App.Api/Services/SessionProjection.cs"],"id":"TASK-3","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":230,"reqs":["REQ-7","REQ-9","REQ-10","REQ-11","REQ-35","REQ-44"],"title":"London time helpers and Session/booking projection"},{"approach":"Methods: GetMember() returns the constant Member(1, \"Alex Rivera\", \"AR\", \"Unlimited Monthly\").\n\nGetSchedule(DateOnly? date, ClassType[]? type, Intensity[]? intensity, TimeOfDay[]? timeOfDay):\n- today is the London date; the current week starts on today's Monday.\n- A date before the current week's Monday or after next week's Sunday → ApiException.Invalid.\n- Days lists Mon–Sun with label \"ddd d\", isToday, and hasSessions = any session starting that London day (filters ignored).\n- Sessions: the selected day's sessions, including studio-cancelled ones. Apply only the filters that are supplied (any-of within a filter, AND across filters). Order by StartsAt.\n- canGoPreviousWeek = weekStart is next week; canGoNextWeek = weekStart is the current week.\n- Each session's demo record is the active Booked/Waitlisted booking for it (latest by id).\n\nGetSession(id) → 404 not_found when missing.\n\nGetMyBookings():\n- upcoming = Booked/Waitlisted records whose session is not studio-cancelled and has not ended (EndsAt > now). Group by London date, label Today / Tomorrow / \"ddd d MMM\", groups ascending, rows by StartsAt.\n- past = Cancelled records (any time), Booked records whose class has ended (shown as Attended), and Booked/Waitlisted records on studio-cancelled sessions (shown as Cancelled by studio), ordered by StartsAt descending.\n- Waitlisted records whose class has ended are omitted.\n\nGetStats():\n- upcoming = Booked records, session not studio-cancelled, now < StartsAt.\n- Attended = Booked records with ended class, session not studio-cancelled.\n- classesThisMonth = Attended records in the current London month.\n- streak = consecutive London weeks with ≥1 Attended record, counted back from the current week, or from the previous week if the current week has none.\n\nListNotices(): Booked records with PromotedAt != null and NoticeAcknowledgedAt == null. Message: \"Good news! You're off the waitlist and booked for {name} · {ddd HH:mm}\".","conventions":["scoped service injected with AppDb, TimeProvider, SessionProjection","AsNoTracking for reads; load the small data set and filter in memory where the filter needs London time","throw ApiException for 400/404"],"dependsOn":["TASK-3"],"exemplars":["App.Api/AppDb.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Services/StudioQueries.cs"],"id":"TASK-4","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":260,"reqs":["REQ-3","REQ-4","REQ-5","REQ-6","REQ-13","REQ-32","REQ-34","REQ-36"],"title":"Read-side queries: member, schedule, session, my bookings, stats, notices"},{"approach":"Create(sessionId) runs these checks in order: not_found → cancelled_by_studio → class_has_started (now ≥ start) → outside_booking_window (start − now > 7d or < 15min) → already_booked (an active Booked/Waitlisted record for this session) → class_full (409 carrying the refreshed Session) → overlap → limit_reached.\n- overlap: compare with Booked records whose session is not studio-cancelled and has not ended, using half-open [start, end). Message: \"You're already booked for {name} at {HH:mm}–{HH:mm}.\"\n- limit_reached: 10 Booked records, not started, session not studio-cancelled. Message: \"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\"\n- On success: insert Booked (CreatedAt = now), BookedCount++, return 201 BookingChange with message \"You're booked for {name} · {ddd HH:mm}\".\n\nJoinWaitlist checks: not_found → cancelled_by_studio → class_has_started → outside_booking_window → already_booked → not_full. On success: position = WaitlistCount + 1, insert Waitlisted, WaitlistCount++, message \"You're on the waitlist for {name} · {ddd HH:mm} — you're #{n}\".\n\nCancel(bookingId): 404 → invalid_booking_state when not Booked (message from the contract example) → class_has_started. On success: Status Cancelled, CancelledAt = now, LateCancel = start − now < 2h. Counts: if WaitlistCount > 0 then WaitlistCount−− (an anonymous member is promoted), else BookedCount−− (floor 0). Message: \"Booking cancelled — {name}, today HH:mm\" when the class is on the current London day, else \"…, ddd HH:mm\".\n\nLeaveWaitlist: 404 → invalid_booking_state when not Waitlisted → class_has_started. On success: Cancelled, LateCancel false, WaitlistPosition null, CancelledAt = now, WaitlistCount−− (floor 0). Message: \"You've left the waitlist for {name}\".\n\nUndo: 404 → invalid_booking_state when not Booked or PromotedAt != null → undo_expired when now − CreatedAt > 5s (message \"Undo is no longer available for this booking.\"). On success: delete the row, BookedCount−−, return UndoResult with message \"Booking undone — {name}\".\n\nSimulate(sessionId): 404 if the session is missing. Let d = the demo member's Waitlisted record on the session.\n- If d is at position 1: d becomes Booked, WaitlistPosition null, PromotedAt = now; WaitlistCount−−. The overlap and limit rules are ignored.\n- Else if WaitlistCount > 0: WaitlistCount−−, and if d exists its position−−.\n- Else: BookedCount−−, never below the demo member's own Booked rows on that session.\n- Return SimulationResult(session, d?.ToBooking or null). The hook is mapped in every environment.\n\nAcknowledge: set NoticeAcknowledgedAt = now on every pending notice.","conventions":["each command runs in one db transaction (BeginTransactionAsync): checks, row change and count change are saved together","rule failures throw ApiException with the contract code and a plain message","messages use LondonTime formatters; em dash '—' and middle dot '·' exactly as in the spec"],"dependsOn":["TASK-3"],"exemplars":["App.Api/AppDb.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Services/BookingCommands.cs"],"id":"TASK-5","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":330,"reqs":["REQ-14","REQ-16","REQ-17","REQ-18","REQ-19","REQ-20","REQ-21","REQ-22","REQ-23","REQ-24","REQ-25","REQ-26","REQ-27","REQ-28","REQ-30","REQ-31","REQ-33","NFR-5"],"title":"Write-side commands: book, waitlist, cancel, leave, undo, simulate, acknowledge"},{"approach":"DatabaseStartup.InitializeDatabase(this WebApplication app):\n- Return immediately when Assembly.GetEntryAssembly()?.GetName().Name == \"GetDocument.Insider\" (this is the build-time document generation run).\n- Otherwise create a scope, call db.Database.EnsureCreated(), and call SampleData.Seed(db, now) only when db.Sessions has no rows.\n- Wrap everything in try/catch and log at Error, so a database that can't be opened doesn't stop startup and requests later fail with 500 storage_failure.\n\nSampleData.Seed:\n- Instructors: 3–5, with name, bio and /avatars/... urls.\n- Sessions: 6–10 in total (inside both the 3–12 and the ≤15 bounds), placed relative to the London date of now:\n  - one later today, bookable;\n  - one yesterday or earlier, already ended, holding a demo Booked record (shown as Attended);\n  - tomorrow, one bookable with spots and one full with WaitlistCount ≥ 2, holding a demo Waitlisted record at position ≤ WaitlistCount;\n  - one in 2 days, studio-cancelled;\n  - one in 3 days, holding a demo Booked record that doesn't overlap anything;\n  - a few more in next week.\n- Set BookedCount to include the demo member's Booked rows and WaitlistCount to include their Waitlisted row.\n- Add the whatToBring items and descriptions.","conventions":["seed times are derived from TimeProvider resolved from app.Services, never from the system clock","stored counts are totals including the demo member's own records"],"dependsOn":["TASK-1","TASK-3"],"exemplars":["App.Api/Program.cs","App.Api/AppDb.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Data/DatabaseStartup.cs","App.Api/Data/SampleData.cs"],"id":"TASK-6","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":170,"reqs":["REQ-39","REQ-40","REQ-41","REQ-42","REQ-43"],"title":"Database startup and sample data seed"},{"approach":"Expose `public static IServiceCollection AddContractOpenApi(this IServiceCollection s)`, which wraps AddOpenApi(o => ...).\n\nDocument transformer:\n- info: title \"Pulse Studio Booking API\", version 1.0.0, plus the description.\n- servers = [ { url: \"/api\" } ].\n- tags: member, schedule, bookings, test-only.\n- components.responses: NotFound, InvalidRequest and StorageFailure, each referencing the Error schema. Point the 400/404/500 responses of operations at them.\n\nSchema transformer, keyed by context.JsonTypeInfo.Type:\n- Set `required` lists exactly as in the contract; ActionState requires only kind and canChange.\n- Add inline enums: ActionState.kind [book, join_waitlist, booked, waitlisted, disabled]; SkipReason.code [overlap, limit_reached, outside_booking_window]; Error.code (13 values); Session.durationMin [30, 45, 60, 75].\n- Wrap ActionState.skipReason, Booking/BookingRow.skipReason, Error.session and SimulationResult.booking as nullable + allOf [$ref].\n- Remove int32 formats so integers are plain `type: integer`.\n- DateOnly → format date; DateTime → format date-time.\n- Make sure the enum schemas (ClassType, Intensity, Room, TimeOfDay, SessionStatus, BookingStatus) become string-enum components with the contract's names and values.\n\nOperation transformer:\n- Response descriptions from the contract.\n- Request body required: true for createBooking and joinWaitlist.\n- Array query params use style form, explode true.\n\nRun dotnet build and diff App.Api/openapi/built.json against the contract until there are 0 differences. Commit the regenerated built.json.","conventions":["only Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 9 transformers (AddDocumentTransformer / AddSchemaTransformer / AddOperationTransformer); no new packages","never read contracts/openapi.yaml at runtime"],"dependsOn":["TASK-2"],"exemplars":["App.Api/App.Api.csproj","App.Api/Program.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/OpenApi/ContractOpenApi.cs","App.Api/openapi/built.json"],"id":"TASK-7","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":220,"reqs":["REQ-1","NFR-6"],"title":"OpenAPI conformance transformers"},{"approach":"Program.cs:\n- Replace AddOpenApi() with AddContractOpenApi().\n- Keep the AddDbContext line. Update the startup comment: the database is now initialised at startup, except under document generation.\n- builder.Services.TryAddSingleton(TimeProvider.System), so a test's replacement wins.\n- Register SessionProjection, StudioQueries and BookingCommands as scoped.\n- Configure<RouteHandlerOptions>(o => o.ThrowOnBadRequest = true).\n- Middleware order: UsePathBase(\"/api\"), then the error handler, then status-code pages, then UseCors. Then map GET /, call app.MapStudioEndpoints(), call app.InitializeDatabase() before app.Run(), and keep `public partial class Program`.\n\nErrorHandling.cs (UseExceptionHandler with a lambda):\n- ApiException → its status + Error(code, message, session).\n- BadHttpRequestException (also when its inner exception is a JsonException) → 400 invalid_request with message \"Something about that request wasn't right. Please try again.\".\n- Anything else → 500 storage_failure with \"We couldn't save your changes just now. Please try again.\". Log the exception server-side only and never write exception text to the response.\n- UseStatusCodePages: when the body is empty, write Error JSON. 404 → not_found; 405 and other 4xx → invalid_request; 5xx → storage_failure.\n\nStudioEndpoints.cs: map all 13 operations with the contract's paths and methods. Use {sessionId:int} and {bookingId:int}. getSchedule binds DateOnly? date, ClassType[]? type, Intensity[]? intensity and TimeOfDay[]? timeOfDay from the query. createBooking and joinWaitlist bind a [FromBody] SessionRequest and return Results.Created with no location (201). acknowledge returns 204. Statuses per operation:\n- getMember 200/500\n- getSchedule 200/400/500\n- getSession 200/404/500\n- createBooking 201/400/404/409/500\n- undo, cancel, leave 200/404/409/500\n- joinWaitlist 201/400/404/409/500\n- getMyBookings, getStats, listPromotionNotices 200/500\n- acknowledge 204/500\n- simulate 200/404/500\nThe simulate hook is mapped in every environment.","conventions":["routes are mapped WITHOUT /api; UsePathBase(\"/api\") serves the prefixed paths","every endpoint has .WithName(operationId) and .WithTags(tag) and declares exactly the contract's statuses via Produces<T>(code) / Produces<Error>(code) / Produces(204)","keep the existing GET / \"API is up\" route with ExcludeFromDescription"],"dependsOn":["TASK-4","TASK-5","TASK-6","TASK-7"],"exemplars":["App.Api/Program.cs"],"fileScope":["App.Api/Endpoints/StudioEndpoints.cs","App.Api/Infrastructure/ErrorHandling.cs","App.Api/Program.cs"],"id":"TASK-8","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":230,"reqs":["REQ-2","REQ-14","REQ-15","REQ-37","REQ-39","REQ-40","REQ-44","NFR-1"],"title":"Endpoints, error handling and Program wiring"}]}